1
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:13,090
Ohm... thump-thump, thump-thump.

2
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:16,270
Heavy stone, solid within.
My skull is forged in steel

3
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:19,930
Against diamond blades,
spears, wooden arrows, and firelocks.

4
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,210
By the power of merit,

5
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:22,180
Magic,

6
00:00:22,423 --> 00:00:24,360
and the essence of a hundred and eight roots.

7
00:00:24,616 --> 00:00:26,860
Descend and dwell within my body.

8
00:00:27,310 --> 00:00:28,866
[Chanting]

9
00:00:29,123 --> 00:00:31,650
[Chanting]

10
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,180
[Chanting]

11
00:00:33,413 --> 00:00:34,596
[Chanting]

12
00:00:34,893 --> 00:00:38,996
From now on.You shall be invulnerable.
No blade can cut you, no bullet can pierce you.

13
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:45,776
Singha.

14
00:00:56,716 --> 00:00:57,243
Mom.

15
00:01:00,096 --> 00:01:01,996
There’s so much you haven't told me, Mom.

16
00:02:10,623 --> 00:02:11,926
There!

17
00:02:12,390 --> 00:02:13,570
What the hell?

18
00:02:14,286 --> 00:02:16,783
What are you spacing out for?
Your mind's already drifted off to the Gulf by now.

19
00:02:17,543 --> 00:02:18,870
Tons of work to do in the shop.

20
00:02:19,136 --> 00:02:20,896
The food’s still not cooked.
When is it going to be ready?

21
00:02:21,563 --> 00:02:24,240
I’m just worried that
Singha won’t come to open the shop

22
00:02:25,133 --> 00:02:25,803
So that’s what you were on about.

23
00:02:26,286 --> 00:02:28,680
Don’t worry. Singha’s gonna show up anyway.

24
00:02:29,066 --> 00:02:30,196
He loves this shop to death.

25
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:31,426
You should worry about yourself instead.

26
00:02:31,786 --> 00:02:33,396
You're so distracted that
no work is getting done.

27
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:37,800
And... aren't you even a bit
curious about where Auntie and Sing went?

28
00:02:38,746 --> 00:02:39,843
No.

29
00:02:40,246 --> 00:02:42,690
Don't want to know. Not my business.

30
00:02:43,233 --> 00:02:43,633
Ok.

31
00:02:44,543 --> 00:02:45,103
But I'm telling you,

32
00:02:45,603 --> 00:02:47,110
Singha wouldn't leave us behind.

33
00:02:47,853 --> 00:02:48,506
And neither would Mae Pim.

34
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:50,020
Think about it.

35
00:02:50,436 --> 00:02:52,693
Without Mae Pim and Singha.

36
00:02:53,336 --> 00:02:56,723
Would you and I even be
standing here, complaining like this? Huh?

37
00:02:56,776 --> 00:02:57,586
Think about it!

38
00:02:58,503 --> 00:02:59,176
Woah, you asshole!

39
00:02:59,506 --> 00:03:00,666
only had one tiny doubt.

40
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:03,153
Way to make me feel guilty for life.

41
00:03:03,356 --> 00:03:05,650
-Unbelievable.
-No more doubts, okay?

42
00:03:05,783 --> 00:03:07,436
Understand? Just get the damn job done.

43
00:03:07,916 --> 00:03:08,640
You.

44
00:03:08,893 --> 00:03:10,456
-Just do your job right.
-Whoa!

45
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:12,820
A new bar just opened up?

46
00:03:13,063 --> 00:03:14,253
Who is it now?

47
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,133
Uh.

48
00:03:21,926 --> 00:03:22,796
We just opened.

49
00:03:27,273 --> 00:03:28,826
Can I get a bottle of beer? You selling yet?

50
00:03:29,393 --> 00:03:30,420
Yep, we're selling.

51
00:03:30,816 --> 00:03:31,980
Small bottles only.

52
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:33,450
Help yourself at the fridge.

53
00:03:33,873 --> 00:03:34,993
First one's 80 baht.

54
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,193
That fridge over there. That one!

55
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:47,723
Whoa.

56
00:03:48,090 --> 00:03:49,800
Look at your face. So fake.

57
00:03:50,353 --> 00:03:51,680
What? Don't be a nosy prick.

58
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:52,560
It's my life.

59
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,236
Is it just the two of you running the place?

60
00:04:03,163 --> 00:04:04,256
Oh, no.

61
00:04:04,706 --> 00:04:06,500
It's a partnership between three of us.

62
00:04:07,446 --> 00:04:08,843
Here, the owner.

63
00:04:09,673 --> 00:04:10,903
And my friends are partners.

64
00:04:11,356 --> 00:04:13,176
And this one? She's the servant.

65
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:14,703
You asshole!

66
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,866
You on vacation, or just here solo?

67
00:04:19,370 --> 00:04:19,776
Oh,

68
00:04:19,823 --> 00:04:21,753
I'm working over at the Amarin Center Hotel.

69
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:23,160
But the manager...

70
00:04:23,743 --> 00:04:25,980
Accused me of being a smart-ass,
so I just quit.

71
00:04:27,803 --> 00:04:28,343
That's good.

72
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:29,583
Now that you've been kicked out,

73
00:04:29,816 --> 00:04:32,653
What’s your next move?
Got another hotel lined up?

74
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,110
No chance.

75
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:37,323
By now, they’ve probably sent
warning letters to every hotel in town.

76
00:04:38,573 --> 00:04:41,073
-Poor soul.
-You freaking flirt.

77
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:44,670
Hey.

78
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:49,290
So.

79
00:04:50,693 --> 00:04:53,373
Are there any job openings here?

80
00:04:56,403 --> 00:04:57,870
What can you do?

81
00:04:58,593 --> 00:04:59,410
Anything you need.

82
00:04:59,993 --> 00:05:03,533
Kitchen, dishes, tables,
DJing, opening up the shop.

83
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:04,966
I can try.

84
00:05:05,593 --> 00:05:06,146
You're in.

85
00:05:07,676 --> 00:05:08,786
Done. Get to it.

86
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:10,433
You.

87
00:05:10,803 --> 00:05:13,436
Go help Mom at the other shop.
You don't need to come here anymore.

88
00:05:13,856 --> 00:05:15,103
I'll stay here with her, just the two of us.

89
00:05:15,476 --> 00:05:16,943
She seems capable. Perfect.

90
00:05:17,493 --> 00:05:18,270
Oh, by the way.

91
00:05:18,976 --> 00:05:20,683
-what's your name?
-I'm Toon.

92
00:05:21,356 --> 00:05:23,053
Toon? Wow, that rhymes with my name!

93
00:05:26,176 --> 00:05:28,113
-ToonJoe, ToonJoe.
-This asshole right here is a total creep.

94
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:29,230
And I'm...

95
00:05:29,533 --> 00:05:29,916
Foon.

96
00:05:32,266 --> 00:05:34,250
JoeToon, JoeToon, Wow.

97
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:35,206
Hey, You.

98
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:37,200
Haven't finished sweeping,
and you're already drinking?

99
00:05:37,446 --> 00:05:38,703
You’re gonna get drunk
and won't be able to sweep.

100
00:05:38,953 --> 00:05:40,230
Ooh, look at you, making that face!

101
00:05:40,746 --> 00:05:42,020
Ugh, picking on me again?

102
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:43,203
Classic you.

103
00:05:55,656 --> 00:05:57,666
This spot is absolutely beautiful.

104
00:05:59,423 --> 00:06:01,536
Thinking of setting up
a dock for international imports.

105
00:06:12,716 --> 00:06:14,710
Those things over there
won't be a problem, right?

106
00:06:17,050 --> 00:06:17,983
That trash pile?

107
00:06:18,883 --> 00:06:19,903
One sweep and it's gone.

108
00:06:22,586 --> 00:06:23,690
Headman Tia’s property.

109
00:06:24,713 --> 00:06:25,763
He's been a thorn in my side.

110
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,950
Next week, an MP is coming down
from Bangkok.

111
00:06:32,423 --> 00:06:34,476
To scout the location and see
about partnering up for the pier.

112
00:06:35,950 --> 00:06:36,836
Everything needs to be kept in order.

113
00:06:39,786 --> 00:06:41,956
These politicians...

114
00:06:42,806 --> 00:06:43,603
They're just greedy bastards.

115
00:06:45,333 --> 00:06:45,740
Right?

116
00:06:47,483 --> 00:06:51,083
Anyway, if you can't talk sense
into them, hand them over to me.

117
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:57,376
These assholes deserve to die with honor.

118
00:07:16,593 --> 00:07:17,410
Why is it so dark?

119
00:07:22,026 --> 00:07:22,680
Where did everyone go?

120
00:07:24,676 --> 00:07:25,006
Hey.

121
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,813
Hey, where did everyone go?

122
00:07:32,663 --> 00:07:34,966
Surprise!

123
00:07:35,273 --> 00:07:38,890
Whoa, look at that! Completely stunned.

124
00:07:40,356 --> 00:07:42,656
Take a good look!
How do you like that? Look at it!

125
00:07:42,830 --> 00:07:45,423
Our work is no joke, you know.

126
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:47,263
Yeah.

127
00:07:47,313 --> 00:07:48,120
Wow.

128
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,800
-You guys are fucking good.
- Yeah, I hear that all the time.

129
00:07:54,930 --> 00:07:57,236
Are you seriously tearing up right now?

130
00:07:58,986 --> 00:07:59,986
It's touching.

131
00:08:01,570 --> 00:08:02,273
Asshole.

132
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:04,686
Man, it's our blood, sweat, and tears.

133
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,746
We were nothing but outcasts.

134
00:08:08,013 --> 00:08:08,973
Always the underdogs.

135
00:08:09,883 --> 00:08:11,066
Who would've thought?

136
00:08:11,423 --> 00:08:13,143
That we could actually build a place like this.

137
00:08:14,266 --> 00:08:14,923
Holy shit!

138
00:08:15,616 --> 00:08:17,420
So fucking awesome!

139
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:19,630
-Well, what are you waiting for? Bring it in!
-Hell yeah!

140
00:08:21,026 --> 00:08:23,583
-You bastard.
-Fucking awesome.

141
00:08:29,850 --> 00:08:31,166
-Hey, Joe.
-Huh?

142
00:08:31,463 --> 00:08:32,736
Is that your girl?

143
00:08:33,026 --> 00:08:33,860
Hell no!

144
00:08:34,663 --> 00:08:35,306
That's Toon.

145
00:08:35,703 --> 00:08:36,656
She just applied for the job today.

146
00:08:36,906 --> 00:08:39,793
You were out, and we had
a spot open. I hired her to help us out.

147
00:08:39,836 --> 00:08:40,280
Yes.

148
00:08:53,510 --> 00:08:55,383
I'm Singha Immortal.

149
00:08:56,883 --> 00:08:57,470
Welcome.

150
00:08:57,806 --> 00:08:59,933
Oh, yeah!

151
00:09:01,623 --> 00:09:02,430
Celebration time!

152
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:07,250
I'll take you guys out for a treat.

153
00:09:08,056 --> 00:09:08,663
Hey.

154
00:09:09,806 --> 00:09:10,480
Joe.

155
00:09:11,653 --> 00:09:13,143
Damn, he’s already passed out.

156
00:09:25,046 --> 00:09:25,746
Singha.

157
00:09:27,503 --> 00:09:28,796
You’ve been gone for so long.

158
00:09:29,883 --> 00:09:32,663
How’d you get so fit?
What have you been doing?

159
00:09:38,393 --> 00:09:39,023
You like it?

160
00:09:52,773 --> 00:09:56,300
I'm just saying you look good, that's all...

161
00:09:57,186 --> 00:09:57,646
Yep.

162
00:09:58,833 --> 00:09:59,490
Look good.

163
00:10:03,873 --> 00:10:06,130
I know you like it.

164
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:10,460
Even while I'm asleep,
I can tell how much of a flirt you are.

165
00:10:10,593 --> 00:10:11,210
Joe.

166
00:10:11,956 --> 00:10:12,806
Not true.

167
00:10:14,753 --> 00:10:16,430
Thanks for nudging me.

168
00:10:16,470 --> 00:10:18,983
Damn, you guys get drunk
and talking like this.

169
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:20,443
Look at how he talks to me.

170
00:10:20,490 --> 00:10:22,696
You should just get drunk and pass out.

171
00:10:23,190 --> 00:10:24,810
Oh, thanks for nudging me twice.

172
00:10:29,776 --> 00:10:30,546
Inspector.

173
00:10:31,150 --> 00:10:33,133
I've found the target now. Name is Singha.

174
00:10:33,343 --> 00:10:34,153
Inside the shop.

175
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:35,746
Just keep an eye on him.

176
00:10:36,326 --> 00:10:37,070
Be careful.

177
00:10:38,546 --> 00:10:39,313
Copy that.

178
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:45,370
What are you doing?

179
00:10:48,746 --> 00:10:49,210
Nothing.

180
00:10:52,243 --> 00:10:52,986
Or you.

181
00:10:54,813 --> 00:10:55,273
Toon.

182
00:10:59,073 --> 00:10:59,563
You.

183
00:11:12,573 --> 00:11:13,830
Foon, you okay?

184
00:11:24,053 --> 00:11:25,943
No need to fear being drunk.

185
00:11:26,236 --> 00:11:27,846
Because we're heavyweight drinker.

186
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:31,550
The face is red only because shy
and embarrassed.

187
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,016
You guys are so cool.

188
00:11:36,496 --> 00:11:37,343
Seem to really love each other.

189
00:11:38,733 --> 00:11:39,640
We grew up together.

190
00:11:40,593 --> 00:11:43,336
Joe and Foon are just kids
from around Walking Street.

191
00:11:45,223 --> 00:11:47,213
Foon's stepfather tried to rape her.

192
00:11:48,853 --> 00:11:50,013
So he ran away from home.

193
00:11:51,316 --> 00:11:52,033
And Joe.

194
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:56,043
His dad would get drunk
and beat the hell out of him.

195
00:11:57,936 --> 00:11:59,456
Great lives they had, right? Real quality stuff.

196
00:12:00,756 --> 00:12:02,673
So, we stick together. Better off this way.

197
00:12:03,956 --> 00:12:04,833
Are you okay?

198
00:12:06,476 --> 00:12:07,093
Me?

199
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:09,066
I have nothing. I'm just...

200
00:12:09,510 --> 00:12:11,063
A piece of shit. Naturally born like this.

201
00:12:16,730 --> 00:12:17,426
How are you a piece of shit?

202
00:12:20,403 --> 00:12:20,976
Forget it.

203
00:12:22,193 --> 00:12:23,390
Living in a shitty city like this.

204
00:12:23,796 --> 00:12:25,040
Being a good person is hard.

205
00:12:26,286 --> 00:12:27,370
But I'm done with all that shit now.

206
00:12:28,110 --> 00:12:29,226
Let's see what happens.

207
00:12:31,056 --> 00:12:33,523
Maybe this shitty city
will become a little less shitty.

208
00:12:37,086 --> 00:12:39,106
Hey, the road is plenty wide!

209
00:12:39,836 --> 00:12:41,736
What's the rush, your dad's funeral? Asshole.

210
00:12:43,023 --> 00:12:43,966
Jackass.

211
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:45,266
Two bikes, just for show.

212
00:12:45,530 --> 00:12:48,416
If I had one, I'd ride seven at once.

213
00:12:49,593 --> 00:12:50,363
Such a shame.

214
00:12:51,016 --> 00:12:52,200
I can't ride a bike.

215
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:54,006
Asshole.

216
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:57,553
Never taken a bus in my life.

217
00:12:59,763 --> 00:13:01,060
Fuck it. That was deep.

218
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:03,263
-Damn!
-Damn it!

219
00:13:17,150 --> 00:13:18,376
Screw you.

220
00:14:06,006 --> 00:14:07,220
Run away!

221
00:14:07,393 --> 00:14:08,936
You’re a traitor.

222
00:14:29,463 --> 00:14:30,190
Hey, what's up?

223
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,323
What the hell is going on?

224
00:15:12,563 --> 00:15:13,616
There's nothing left.

225
00:15:19,166 --> 00:15:20,906
Who the fuck did this? Motherfucker!

226
00:15:21,996 --> 00:15:23,006
If I ever find out who it was.

227
00:15:23,893 --> 00:15:26,233
I'll fucking kill them all.

228
00:15:30,070 --> 00:15:30,856
Fuck!

229
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:43,113
You son of a bitch!

230
00:15:55,146 --> 00:15:56,630
It's been taken care of, boss.

231
00:15:59,263 --> 00:16:00,953
There won't be
any trouble from this Village Chief, right?

232
00:16:01,426 --> 00:16:01,846
Yes, sir.

233
00:16:05,783 --> 00:16:06,876
Probably won't use

234
00:16:07,576 --> 00:16:09,033
The rubber plantation as a graveyard.

235
00:16:09,623 --> 00:16:10,870
I said I'm not selling!

236
00:16:11,476 --> 00:16:13,110
What part of no don't you get?

237
00:16:13,536 --> 00:16:15,976
Go tell your boss
to stay the hell away from me!

238
00:16:16,356 --> 00:16:17,846
I'm being respectful to you, sir.

239
00:16:18,730 --> 00:16:20,793
Why do you have to be
so aggressive with me?

240
00:16:21,423 --> 00:16:22,606
So, you're not selling.

241
00:16:24,453 --> 00:16:25,756
I said I won't sell!

242
00:16:26,293 --> 00:16:27,926
Get out! Now!

243
00:16:48,376 --> 00:16:49,536
The rubber isn't even selling well.

244
00:16:50,526 --> 00:16:51,253
How pitiful.

245
00:16:52,586 --> 00:16:54,476
But he just won't listen. Stubborn as hell.

246
00:16:59,770 --> 00:17:00,530
Yes, Mr. Vinit.

247
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:04,160
Everything is settled, sir.

248
00:17:05,486 --> 00:17:08,500
No need to call me yourself. I feel bad.

249
00:17:11,696 --> 00:17:12,386
Yes, you can come.

250
00:17:13,293 --> 00:17:14,353
Oh, please come, sir.

251
00:17:15,603 --> 00:17:17,346
It won't be dull, sir.
Definitely not a dull moment.

252
00:17:17,583 --> 00:17:18,610
I'll have people ready for you.

253
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:21,600
I guarantee there will be
plenty of people giving you flowers.

254
00:17:23,796 --> 00:17:25,630
Yes, sir. I'll take care of it. Goodbye, sir.

255
00:17:28,726 --> 00:17:29,220
Go.

256
00:17:32,290 --> 00:17:33,160
Dammit!

257
00:17:34,663 --> 00:17:36,640
Always demanding shit
but never spends a goddamn penny.

258
00:17:37,716 --> 00:17:38,420
Damn you, Vinit.

259
00:17:39,293 --> 00:17:40,213
This has happened way too many times now.

260
00:17:42,390 --> 00:17:43,563
You...

261
00:17:44,263 --> 00:17:45,783
You're a real piece of work, you know that?

262
00:17:46,723 --> 00:17:47,903
Aren't you afraid of karma at all?

263
00:17:48,276 --> 00:17:48,916
Oh, please!

264
00:17:49,850 --> 00:17:50,526
Why should I be afraid?

265
00:17:51,216 --> 00:17:52,723
Who knows if heaven and hell even exist.

266
00:17:53,890 --> 00:17:54,753
It's about the present moment.

267
00:17:55,383 --> 00:17:57,026
Money, power.

268
00:17:57,670 --> 00:17:58,273
I need it all.

269
00:17:59,836 --> 00:18:01,100
Impressive.

270
00:18:02,030 --> 00:18:04,650
Just the kind of person
the world needs right now.

271
00:18:05,696 --> 00:18:06,243
Why?

272
00:18:07,426 --> 00:18:08,920
Is someone like me really that important?

273
